From: klizas <lukas@klizas.lt>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/appletbdrm: allocate the framebuffer request with kzalloc

begin_fb_access() allocates the whole framebuffer request with
kvzalloc() and later sends it with usb_bulk_msg(). A full-frame request
is several hundred KiB, so when memory is fragmented kvzalloc() falls
back to vmalloc(). The USB core maps the transfer buffer with
dma_map_single(), which refuses vmalloc memory, the URB is never
submitted and the frame is dropped:

  apple-bce 0000:04:00.1: rejecting DMA map of vmalloc memory
  WARNING: ./include/linux/dma-mapping.h:524 at dma_map_single_attrs+0x86/0xc0
   usb_hcd_map_urb_for_dma+0x36c/0x3f0
   usb_start_wait_urb+0x8f/0x1d0
   appletbdrm_primary_plane_helper_atomic_update+0x311/0x400 [appletbdrm]

USB transfer buffers must be physically contiguous. Allocate the request
with kzalloc() and free it with kfree(). Unlike the kmalloc attempt
inside kvzalloc(), a plain GFP_KERNEL allocation compacts memory before
it gives up, and a failure makes the commit return -ENOMEM instead of
dropping the frame later.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/appletbdrm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/appletbdrm.c
@@ -339,7 +339,7 @@
 	if (!(request_size % SZ_512))
 		request_size += 16;
 
-	appletbdrm_state->request = kvzalloc(request_size, GFP_KERNEL);
+	appletbdrm_state->request = kzalloc(request_size, GFP_KERNEL);
 
 	if (!appletbdrm_state->request)
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -552,7 +552,7 @@
 {
 	struct appletbdrm_plane_state *appletbdrm_state = to_appletbdrm_plane_state(state);
 
-	kvfree(appletbdrm_state->request);
+	kfree(appletbdrm_state->request);
 	kfree(appletbdrm_state->response);
 
 	__drm_gem_destroy_shadow_plane_state(&appletbdrm_state->base);
